ilure in failures:\n    print(\"FAIL:\", failure)\nprint(f\"{checks} full-game network checks, {len(failures)} failures\")\nraise SystemExit(bool(failures))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_52","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\np='Son-of-a-Sun-Superman-1979-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-011205/run-tests.py'\ns=open(p).read().replace('r\\\"(\\\\\\\\d+) checks?,\\\\\\\\s*(\\\\\\\\d+) failures?\\\"','r\\\"(\\\\\\\\d+) [\"'^'\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\d]*checks?,\\\\\\\\s*(\\\\\\\\d+) failures?\\\"')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nimport json\np='exit-interview.json'\nd=json.load(open(p));d['testingFeedback']=['Testing and static review caught 4 implementation issues; all were fixed. Incorrect expectations in test scripts were corrected separately and are not counted as game issues.','3 were startup or co-op breaking: bundled helper-name collisions, missing network actor setup, and GPU warmup exceeding the Hub ready deadline. The fourth omitted guest enemy visuals.','The complete scripted campaign exercised actual powers and sunlight recharge, while the official stressed four-player Hub harness exposed integration timing. Travel was accelerated with developer teleports.','Early software-WebGPU screenshots were blank and could not assess art. The same scene was reviewed using the optional WebGL compatibility renderer.']\nd['engineFeedback']=['Three.js TSL makes a genuine three-band cel shader straightforward, and AnimationMixer provides clean native flight and cape animation. Rapier gives solid sliding collision during free flight.','The initial single-file concatenation collided on common helper names. Waiting for an optional full shader precompile also caused Hub ready deadlines to expire; isolated module scopes and lazy GPU compilation fixed both.','The superhero flight controller, rescue and power interactions, mission state machine, TV-scale menu focus, touch assistance, procedural city, code audio, and authoritative multiplayer snapshots.','Coordinating browser GPU startup, physics authority, remote visual state and a standalone single-file package. Software-WebGPU screenshot capture in this environment remains unreliable.','none','A first-class asynchronous first-frame readiness and GPU diagnostic API that works reliably in automated browser tests.']\nd['promptFeedback']=['The source-first brief and controller-first requirements encouraged a coherent rescue game rather than a disconnected feature showcase.','The title and year alone leave the precise source edition ambiguous. I used the 1979 game’s city-rescue, green danger, bridge and telephone-booth ideas with the broader Superman tone; the intended exact edition is unknown.','Delivering a whole mission arc with enjoyable free flight, multiple co-op transports, usable touch assistance and one shareable HTML file.','Name the exact source edition and distinguish required cross-device networking from same-device co-op; specify whether a hosted signaling or TURN service is available.']\nd['sourceInformation']['testing']='Consolidated automated suite: native WebGPU state, full scripted campaign and bridge bonus, physics, menus, balance controls, simulated standard gamepad, touch, OfflineAudioContext, file:// boot, WebRTC/BroadcastChannel and official 4-player Hub stress/server/host-leave harness. Visual art reviewed through optional WebGL compatibility backend. Real controller, separate-device NAT and audible listening: unknown.'\njson.dump(d,open(p,'w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False);open(p,'a').write('\\\\n')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
